--TEST--
`Core\Http\Client::openSocket` refuses a `protocols` entry that is not one RFC 6455 subprotocol token — empty, a comma, a space, a control byte or a non-ASCII letter — and a scripted peer refuses it exactly as a live handshake does — `rule:http-server/an-outbound-socket-is-opened-like-an-outbound-call`, `rule:testing/an-outbound-socket-is-answered-by-a-scripted-peer`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Http\Socket::protocol
// A bound asserted on both sides: the widest token RFC 7230 allows is offered
// and read back unchanged, and every entry one character outside it is refused
// before any peer is asked. The names travel joined by `, ` in one header, so
// `a,b` offered as one name would reach the peer as two, and a line break
// would end the header. The scripted peer chooses each bad name, so a
// refusal here cannot be `settled` refusing a name that was never offered.
Core\Test::answerSocket("wss://gateway.example.com/wide", [], {protocol: "A-z.0_9!#$%&'*+^`|~"});
var $wide = Core\Http\Client::openSocket("wss://gateway.example.com/wide", {
    protocols: ["A-z.0_9!#$%&'*+^`|~"],
});
echo "accepted: ", $wide->protocol() ?? "none", "\n";

array<string> $bad = ["", "a,b", "two words", "line\r\nX-Injected: yes", "tab\there", "é", "semi;colon"];
var $refused = 0;
var $n = 0;
foreach ($bad as string $name) {
    string $url = "wss://gateway.example.com/bad/" . $n;
    $n = $n + 1;
    Core\Test::answerSocket($url, [], {protocol: $name});
    try {
        Core\Http\Client::openSocket($url, {protocols: ["chat.v1", $name]});
    } catch (RuntimeError $error) {
        $refused = $refused + 1;
    }
}
echo "refused: ", $refused, " of ", $n, "\n";

// The refusal names the entry, escaped, so a line break in it is visible.
try {
    Core\Http\Client::openSocket("wss://gateway.example.com/bad/3", {protocols: ["line\r\nX: y"]});
} catch (RuntimeError $shown) {
    echo $shown->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
accepted: A-z.0_9!#$%&'*+^`|~
refused: 7 of 7
Core\Http\Client::openSocket: "line\r\nX: y" is not a subprotocol name — a name is one word of letters, digits and the characters !#$%&'*+-.^_`|~, with no space, comma or control character
